/*  Types, where a type is written — ParseTypeAnnotationCore and its neighbours in
    `src/Interpreter/Parser.cs`.

    A type is a node like any other, named after the C# class it stands for: `(NumberType)`,
    `(SeriesType (TextType))`, `(ObjectType "stack" [(NumberType)])`.

    ⚠ The C# parser marks a type position with a depth it restores in a `finally`. Here a failure
    ends the whole file, so only the SPECULATIVE parses — which catch a failure and go on — restore
    anything, and they restore the depth along with the position.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Bind node to plain-type, given (the text kind):
        Return cast made on (kind, a series of node).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to type-annotation unto parser:
        Increment one's type-depth by 1.
        Define parsed as cast one's type-core or pass the failure off.
        Decrement one's type-depth by 1.
        Return parsed.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to type-core unto parser:
        Define tok as cast one's peek.
        Define kind as tok's kind.

        If kind is "Void":
            Cast one's advance.
            Return cast plain-type on ("VoidType").
        Done.

        If kind is "Record" or cast spelled on (tok, "records"):
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Like") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Return cast one's record-shape-body or pass the failure off.
        Done.

        // (A or B or C), and (T or void) is a voidable T.
        If kind is "LParen":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define cases as cast listed.
            Define first-case as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Cast cases's add on (first-case).
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            While cast one's peek-kind is "Or", repeat:
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define next-case as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
                Cast cases's add on (next-case).
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Cast one's consume on ("RParen") or pass the failure off.
            If the number of cases's children is 2:
                Define one-case as item 1 of cases's children.
                Define other-case as item 2 of cases's children.
                If one-case's kind is "VoidType":
                    Return cast made on ("VoidableType", a series with (other-case)).
                Done.
                If other-case's kind is "VoidType":
                    Return cast made on ("VoidableType", a series with (one-case)).
                Done.
            Done.
            Return cast made on ("UnionType", a series with (cases)).
        Done.

        If kind is "Voidable":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define inner as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            // A voidable never nests: voidable voidable T is voidable T.
            If inner's kind is "VoidableType", return inner.
            Return cast made on ("VoidableType", a series with (inner)).
        Done.

        If kind is "SetKw":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define element as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Return cast made on ("SetType", a series with (element)).
        Done.

        If kind is "Map":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("From") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define key-type as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("To") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define value-type as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Return cast made on ("MapType", a series with (key-type, value-type)).
        Done.

        If kind is "NumberKw" or (kind is "Identifier" and cast spelled on (tok, "numbers")):
            Cast one's advance.
            Return cast plain-type on ("NumberType").
        Done.
        If kind is "Identifier":
            Define lowered as tok's lexeme in lowercase.
            If lowered is "text" or lowered is "texts":
                Cast one's advance.
                Return cast plain-type on ("TextType").
            Done.
            If lowered is "fact" or lowered is "facts":
                Cast one's advance.
                Return cast plain-type on ("FactType").
            Done.
            If lowered is "address" or lowered is "addresses":
                Cast one's advance.
                Return cast plain-type on ("AddressType").
            Done.
            If lowered is "bits":
                Cast one's advance.
                Return cast plain-type on ("BitsType").
            Done.
        Done.

        If kind is "Series":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define element as cast one's element-type on (true) or pass the failure off.
            Return cast made on ("SeriesType", a series with (element)).
        Done.

        If kind is "Stash":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define element as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Return cast made on ("StashType", a series with (element)).
        Done.

        If cast spelled on (tok, "readable") or cast spelled on (tok, "writable"):
            Define stream-kind as "ReadableStreamType" when cast spelled on (tok, "readable"), otherwise "WritableStreamType".
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Stream") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define element as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Return cast made on (stream-kind, a series with (element)).
        Done.

        If kind is "Channel" or (cast spelled on (tok, "channel") and cast one's kind-after is "Of"):
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define element as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Return cast made on ("ChannelType", a series with (element)).
        Done.

        If cast spelled on (tok, "matrix") or cast spelled on (tok, "matrices"):
            Cast one's advance.
            Return cast plain-type on ("MatrixType").
        Done.
        If cast spelled on (tok, "chase"):
            Cast one's advance.
            Return cast plain-type on ("ChaseType").
        Done.

        // catalogue [of T] — a series whose elements are a union; atlas [from K to V] — a map.
        If kind is "CatalogueKw":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Of":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define element as cast one's element-type on (true) or pass the failure off.
                Return cast made on ("SeriesType", a series with (element)).
            Done.
            Return cast made on ("SeriesType", a series with (cast open-union)).
        Done.
        If kind is "AtlasKw":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "From":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define key-type as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("To") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define value-type as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
                Return cast made on ("MapType", a series with (key-type, value-type)).
            Done.
            Return cast made on ("MapType", a series with (cast plain-type on ("TextType"), cast open-union)).
        Done.

        // `<language> [<result>] [axiom] [given (…)]` — foreign source, tagged by its language.
        If kind is "Identifier" and (cast one's next-word-is on ("axiom") or cast one's is-axiom-result-ahead):
            Define axiom-type as cast one's axiom-type-after-tag on (tok) or pass the failure off.
            If axiom-type's word is not "_", return axiom-type.
        Done.

        // A named type — an object or interface, with its blanks filled: `a stack of number`.
        If kind is "Identifier":
            Cast one's advance.
            Define args as cast listed.
            While cast one's peek-kind is "Of", repeat:
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define argument as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
                Cast args's add on (argument).
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Return cast made on ("ObjectType", a series with (cast quoted on (tok's lexeme), args)).
        Done.

        Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (tok,
            "type name (number, text, fact, series of ..., or a defined type name)")).
    Done.

    /// The axiom arm of ParseTypeAnnotationCore. Nothing, with the position put back, when what
    /// looked like a result type was the name being declared all along.
    Bind node or failure to axiom-type-after-tag unto parser, given (the token tag):
        Define saved-at as one's at.
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define before-result as one's at.
        Define saved-depth as one's type-depth.
        Define result as cast nothing.
        If cast one's is-word on ("axiom") is false:
            Try to:
                The result becomes cast one's type-annotation.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            In case of failure:
                If (the first 11 characters of the message of the failure) is "unsupported":
                    Return a failure (the message of the failure).
                Done.
                One's at becomes before-result.
                One's type-depth becomes saved-depth.
                The result becomes cast nothing.
            Done.
        Done.
        If cast one's is-word on ("axiom"):
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Otherwise if result's word is not "_" and cast one's peek-kind is not "Identifier" and cast one's peek-kind is not "Given":
            One's at becomes before-result.
            The result becomes cast nothing.
        Done.
        Define takes as cast listed.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Given":
            The takes becomes cast one's function-param-type-list or pass the failure off.
            If the number of takes's children is greater than 0, cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        If result's word is not "_" or the number of takes's children is greater than 0 or cast one's peek-kind is "Identifier":
            Return cast made on ("AxiomType", a series with (cast quoted on (tag's lexeme), result, takes)).
        Done.
        One's at becomes saved-at.
        Return cast nothing.
    Done.

    /// IsAxiomResultAhead — a language tag followed by a result type.
    Bind fact to is-axiom-result-ahead unto parser:
        Define here as cast one's peek.
        If here's kind is "Identifier":
            Define lowered as here's lexeme in lowercase.
            If lowered is "c-language" or lowered is "cufet" or lowered is "regex", return true.
        Done.
        Define next-tok as cast one's token-at on (cast one's past-noise on (one's at + 1)).
        Define next-kind as next-tok's kind.
        If next-kind is "NumberKw" or next-kind is "Void" or next-kind is "Voidable", return true.
        If next-kind is "Identifier":
            Define lowered as next-tok's lexeme in lowercase.
            Return lowered is "text" or lowered is "fact" or lowered is "bits".
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// The element type after `of`, where a function type may be the element.
    Bind node or failure to element-type unto parser, given (the fact name-follows):
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Void":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("FunctionKw") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define parameters as cast one's function-param-type-list or pass the failure off.
            Return cast made on ("FunctionType", a series with (parameters, cast nothing)).
        Done.
        Define inner as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "FunctionKw", return inner.
        If name-follows and cast one's kind-after is not "Given", return inner.
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define parameters as cast one's function-param-type-list or pass the failure off.
        Return cast made on ("FunctionType", a series with (parameters, inner)).
    Done.

    /// `given (<type>, …)` in a function type — empty when there is no `given`.
    Bind node or failure to function-param-type-list unto parser:
        Define types as cast listed.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "Given", return types.
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("LParen") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "RParen":
            Define first-type as cast one's function-param-type or pass the failure off.
            Cast types's add on (first-type).
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            While cast one's peek-kind is "Comma", repeat:
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define next-type as cast one's function-param-type or pass the failure off.
                Cast types's add on (next-type).
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("RParen") or pass the failure off.
        Return types.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to function-param-type unto parser:
        Increment one's type-depth by 1.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define returned as cast nothing.
        Define saw-void as false.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Void":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            The saw-void becomes true.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            The returned becomes cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "FunctionKw":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define parameters as cast one's function-param-type-list or pass the failure off.
            Decrement one's type-depth by 1.
            Return cast made on ("FunctionType", a series with (parameters, returned)).
        Done.
        If saw-void:
            Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek,
                "function — 'void' can only appear as a function return type")).
        Done.
        Decrement one's type-depth by 1.
        Return returned.
    Done.

    // ── Record shapes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `(<positional types>, the <type> <name>, …)`. ⚠ The named fields come out SORTED by name,
    /// because RecordType sorts them — two shapes are equal whatever order their fields were written.
    Bind node or failure to record-shape-body unto parser:
        Return cast one's shape-into on (cast listed, cast listed) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// A record shape, also collecting the names declared `permanently` and the fields given a
    /// default — which an object definition keeps and a plain record type does not.
    Bind node or failure to shape-into unto parser, given (the node permanent, the node defaults):
        Cast one's consume on ("LParen") or pass the failure off.
        Define positional as cast listed.
        Define named as cast listed.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "RParen":
            Cast one's one-shape-field on (positional, named, permanent, defaults) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            While cast one's peek-kind is "Comma", repeat:
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's one-shape-field on (positional, named, permanent, defaults) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("RParen") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast made on ("RecordType", a series with (positional, cast sorted-by-name on (named))).
    Done.

    /// The pairs of a list, ordered by the quoted name each begins with.
    ///
    /// ⚠ Through `sorted by` on records, because `is less than` does not order text.
    Bind node to sorted-by-name, given (the node pairs):
        Define keyed as a series of records like (the text name, the number spot).
        Define spot as 0.
        For each pair in pairs's children, repeat:
            Increment spot by 1.
            Define first-part as item 1 of pair's children.
            Insert a record with (the name first-part's word, the spot spot) into keyed.
        Done.
        Define ordered as cast listed.
        For each entry in keyed sorted by name, repeat:
            Cast ordered's add on (item (the spot of entry) of pairs's children).
        Done.
        Return ordered.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to one-shape-field unto parser, given (the node positional, the node named, the node permanent, the node defaults):
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Article":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define void-return as cast one's peek-kind is "Void".
            Define returned as cast nothing.
            If void-return:
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The returned becomes cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Define is-function as cast one's peek-kind is "FunctionKw".
            If void-return and is-function is false:
                Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek,
                    "field — 'void' can only appear as a function return type")).
            Done.
            If is-function:
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Define name-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
            Define field-type as returned.
            If is-function:
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define parameters as cast one's function-param-type-list or pass the failure off.
                The field-type becomes cast made on ("FunctionType", a series with (parameters, returned)).
            Done.
            Define pair as cast listed.
            Cast pair's add on (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme)).
            Cast pair's add on (field-type).
            Cast named's add on (pair).
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Permanently":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast permanent's add on (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme)).
            Done.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "With":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                If cast one's is-word on ("default") is false:
                    Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek,
                        "field '{name-tok's lexeme}' — 'with' here introduces a default, so write "
                        joined to "'the ... {name-tok's lexeme} with default <value>'")).
                Done.
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define fallback as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Define default-pair as cast listed.
                Cast default-pair's add on (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme)).
                Cast default-pair's add on (fallback).
                Cast defaults's add on (default-pair).
            Done.
            Return.
        Done.
        If the number of named's children is greater than 0:
            Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek,
                "type — positional fields must come before named fields in a record shape")).
        Done.
        Define field-type as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
        Cast positional's add on (field-type).
    Done.

    /// TryParseTypeBeforeName — a type, when a NAME follows it; otherwise nothing, and the position
    /// put back.
    ///
    /// ⚠ Only a REFUSAL rolls back. A construct this parser has not been taught yet is not "no type
    /// here" — rolling that back would read the tag of `Define regex serious as […]` as the name.
    Bind node or failure to type-before-name unto parser:
        Define saved-at as one's at.
        Define saved-depth as one's type-depth.
        Increment one's type-depth by 1.
        Try to:
            Define parsed as cast one's type-annotation.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Identifier":
                One's type-depth becomes saved-depth.
                Return parsed.
            Done.
        Done.
        In case of failure:
            If (the first 11 characters of the message of the failure) is "unsupported":
                Return a failure (the message of the failure).
            Done.
        Done.
        One's at becomes saved-at.
        One's type-depth becomes saved-depth.
        Return cast nothing.
    Done.
Done.
